%S A400996 1,1,3,12,50,210,884,3724,15692,66128,278680,1174440,4949456,20858576,
%T A400996 87904688,370458432,1561230240,6579523360,27728215104,116855564224,
%U A400996 492466711232,2075412183808,8746450541440,36860339200640,155341255239936,654657718917376
%N A400996 Number of fixed point free involutions in S_{2n} (or perfect matchings on [2n]) which avoid the patterns {123, 231, 321}.
%C A400996 a(n) is the number of perfect matchings on [2n] that simultaneously avoid the patterns 123, 231, and 321, where pattern avoidance for matchings is in the sense of Bloom and Elizalde. The term a(0)=1 corresponds to the empty matching.
%H A400996 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400996/b400996.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A400996 Sucharita Biswas, Umesh Shankar and Sivaramakrishnan Sivasubramanian, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08562">Matchings and shape-Wilf-Equivalence of sets of patterns of length three I: Triples</a>, arXiv:2609.08562 [math.CO], 2026. See Theorem 26.
%H A400996 Jonathan Bloom and Sergi Elizalde, <a href="https://doi.org/10.37236/2976">Pattern avoidance in matchings and partitions</a>, The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, 20(2) (2013), #P5.
%H A400996 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (6,-8,2).
%F A400996 G.f.: (1 - 5*x + 5*x^2)/(1 - 6*x + 8*x^2 - 2*x^3).
%F A400996 a(0)=1, a(1)=1, a(2)=3, and for n >= 3, a(n) = 6*a(n-1) - 8*a(n-2) + 2*a(n-3).
%t A400996 LinearRecurrence[{6, -8, 2}, {1, 1, 3}, 30] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 19 2026 *)
%Y A400996 Cf. A399989 (avoiding the patterns 132, 312, and 321).
%K A400996 nonn,easy,new
%O A400996 0,3
%A A400996 _Sucharita Biswas_, Oct 12 2026
